WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.501 --> 00:00:03.086
- All right!
Hey, palsies!

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:05.255
My name is Cody,
and I'm a Helpster.

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:07.174
That means a monster who helps.

00:00:07.257 --> 00:00:10.969
And because I love, love, love
to help so much,

00:00:11.053 --> 00:00:12.930
I'm making these videos called...

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:20.354
Guess what?
Today, I am gonna teach you

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:22.064
how to be a Helpster.

00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:24.983
So, a Helpster
is a monster who helps,

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:29.196
so job one is...
be a monster.

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:31.323
So, how do you do that,
you might ask.

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:32.824
Well, um, let's see.

00:00:32.908 --> 00:00:36.995
Oh, monsters love to smile,
so you gotta smile.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:38.163
Like this.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.416
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm. Good!

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.709
Ok, let's see. What else?

00:00:42.793 --> 00:00:47.005
Ooh! Ooh. Monsters can move
really fast. Like this.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.675
And this.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:51.343
And this!

00:00:51.844 --> 00:00:55.514
Like that.
And Monsters love to dance.

00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:56.515
Like this.

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:59.601
[music plays]

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.023
And last, but not least,

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:08.068
Monsters love to sing.
Like this.

00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:10.445
♪ Boppity-bop-bop,
boo-dee-doh ♪

00:01:10.529 --> 00:01:12.322
♪ I love to sing ♪

00:01:12.406 --> 00:01:13.574
Yeah!

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:14.950
[audience applauding]

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.743
Oh, thank you.
That's very kind of you.

00:01:16.827 --> 00:01:20.247
Congratulations!
You're a monster.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:23.166
Now, job two
is to find a way to help.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.752
And I have a few ideas.

00:01:25.836 --> 00:01:28.839
You can put your toys away, or you can
put books back on the bookshelf,

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.884
or hang up your coat,
or put dirty clothes in the hamper,

00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:35.012
or, uh, or you could help cheer
someone up by playing with them.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.181
Or-or, if someone needs quiet time,

00:01:37.264 --> 00:01:38.974
you can help by playing by yourself.

00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:42.978
Ooh-ooh! Or, you can do
my favorite thing ever,

00:01:43.061 --> 00:01:46.899
which is...
ask someone how you can help.

00:01:46.982 --> 00:01:50.027
-[cell phone rings]
-Oh. Oh, excuse me just a moment. Uh...

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.403
Hello?

00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:53.572
- Cody, it's Mr. Prim.

00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:56.325
I am in need of your help.

00:01:56.408 --> 00:01:58.493
- Ooh, well, of course, Mr. Prim.

00:01:58.577 --> 00:02:00.996
Let me just say good-bye
to everybody first.

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:03.165
- Uh, good-bye?
Good-bye to whom?

00:02:03.248 --> 00:02:06.543
Oh, well, you see, I'm making
these little videos right now,

00:02:06.627 --> 00:02:09.296
and I just wanted to tell
everyone watching to make sure they help

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:12.883
the people and monsters around them,
'cause everyone loves a helping hand.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:16.678
- Hmm. I believe
you just did tell them that.

00:02:17.596 --> 00:02:20.265
- Oh, yeah! Ha!

00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:21.892
See you next time, everybody!

